# SUPERSEDED — DO NOT INSTALL. Use packaging/udev/72-hyprpad-puck.rules instead.
#
# The number below is wrong, and the reason is the whole point of the newer file.
# `TAG+="uaccess"` grants nothing by itself; the ACL is applied by systemd's
# 73-seat-late.rules (`TAG=="uaccess" … RUN{builtin}+="uaccess"`), and `man udev`
# says a RUN entry is "executed after processing of all the rules for the event".
# So by the time a 99- rule runs, the builtin has already been queued and this
# file's `TAG-="uaccess"` changes nothing — the session user keeps an ACL that
# beats the MODE/GROUP set here. The removal must land BEFORE 73-seat-late.rules.
#
# Kept only as the W12 experiment's record. See docs/design/uhid-relay.md §6.1.
#
# W12 reference rule — hand the 2026 Steam Controller puck to hyprpad, not the
# session user. Ordered 99- so it runs after Steam's 60-steam-input.rules (which
# adds MODE=0660 + TAG+="uaccess") and after 70-uaccess.rules.
#
# Effect: strip the uaccess tag (so logind stops ACL-granting the node to the
# active-session user — which is how BOTH Steam and a session-user process get
# access today), and assign the node to a dedicated `hyprpad` group. Only a
# process in that group (the privileged hyprpad daemon) can then open it; Steam,
# running as the ordinary session user, cannot — and instead sees the virtual
# controller hyprpad emits.
#
# Requires: a `hyprpad` group, and hyprpad running as a member of it (system
# daemon or setgid helper) — NOT as the plain session user, because the session
# user is exactly who must be denied.
#
# INSTALL:  sudo groupadd -r hyprpad
#           sudo cp 99-hyprpad-claim-puck.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#           sudo udevadm control --reload
#           sudo udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=hidraw   # or replug the puck
# REVERT:   sudo rm /etc/udev/rules.d/99-hyprpad-claim-puck.rules && \
#           sudo udevadm control --reload && (replug puck)
#
# Match both the hidraw nodes and the parent so all interface slots are covered.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="28de", ATTRS{idProduct}=="1304", \
  TAG-="uaccess", GROUP="hyprpad", MODE="0660"
